<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tofangchi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tofangchi were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musket">musketeers</a> in the armies of Safavid and later Iranian states. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a> they were organised as a corps paid directly from the royal treasury and loyal to the Shah rather than to tribal chiefs. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zand-dynasty">Zand Empire</a> also recruited Persian tofangchi to supplement its tribal cavalry and infantry, as described in its profile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tofangchi.jpg" alt="Tofangchi" width="218" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Habib Allah Mashadi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Persian_Musketeer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
